  "texts": {
    "preamble": "V.P. Mathew vs Food Inspector on 4 February, 2016 Author: B.Sudheendra Kumar Bench: B.Sudheendra Kumar In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present: The Honourable Mr. Justice B.Sudheendra Kumar Thursday, The 4Th Day Of February 2016/15Th Magha, 1937 Crl.Rev.Pet.No. 256 of 2005 ( ) -------------------------------- Cra 111/2003 of 5 Addl.Sessions Judge, Ernakulam Cc 286/1999 of J.M.F.C.-I,Kochi Revision Petitioner/Apellant/Accused No.1:: ---------------------------------------------------------------------- V.P. Mathew, Vattatharakooram, Edavanakkad. By Adv. Sri.N.A.Muraleedharan Respondents/Complainant & State:: ----------------------------------------------------------- 1. Food Inspector, Cochin Circle. 2. State Of Kerala Represented By The Public Prosecutor, High Court, Of Kerala Ernakulam. R1 & R2 By Public Prosecutor, Shri.R.Githesh This Criminal Revision Petition Having Been Finally Heard On 04-02-2016, The Court On The Same Day Passed The Following: B.Sudheendra Kumar, J. - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -- - - -- - - - - - - - - - -- - - - - - - - - Crl.R.P. No.256 of 2005 V.P. Mathew vs Food Inspector on 4 February, 2016 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/105892870/ 1 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - Dated this the 4th day of February 2016 O R D E R",
    "facts": "The prosecution allegation can be briefly stated thus:- On 4.3.1999 at 5.30 p.m., PW1, the Food Inspector, purchased 750 gram of gingelly oil from the shop of the revision petitioner. After sampling as per rules, one of the samples was sent for analysis to the Public Analyst. The Public Analyst filed Ext. P22 report stating that the sample did not conform to the standard prescribed for gingelly oil under the Prevention of Food Adulteration Rules, 1955 and therefore, the same was adulterated. 4. Before the trial Court, PW1 to 5 were examined and Exts.P1 to P26 were marked for the prosecution. DW1 was examined and Exts.D1 and D2 were marked for the revision petitioner. It is borne out from the records that the revision petitioner renewed the license on 31.3.1999. PW1 purchased the food article on 4.3.1999.",
